# ── SPA fallback (catch-all) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Physical prerendered files (dist/fr/index.html etc.) are served FIRST by
# Cloudflare Pages, before any _redirects rule — so every indexable page is a
# real static 200. For routes that are valid but NOT prerendered at scale
# (non-allowlisted A-vs-B comparisons, be/at blog that reuses fr/de, blog
# category hubs, cards unavailable in a market…), serve the SPA shell at 200 so
# the client renders the right page. Previously this was `/404.html 404`, but on
# Cloudflare Pages the per-path `… /index.html 200` rewrites above were NOT
# honored, so every non-prerendered route returned a hard 404 while the SPA
# still booted from 404.html — i.e. real content served with a 404 status.
# The not-found state of every page type is noindex (BlogPost, ReviewPage,
# CardDetail, ComparisonPage non-allowlisted, BrandPage empty, NotFound), so a
# genuinely dead URL resolves to 200 + noindex (dropped cleanly) instead of a
# soft 404 on content Googlebot can see.
/*  /index.html  200
